        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.317,
            0.107,
            0.584,
            0.13
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "The Journey Beyond"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.118,
            0.165,
            0.775,
            0.201
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "y Read about the ‘Seed Village Programme’ (Beej Gram Yojana) run by the Government of India. Why is it important to save indigenous seeds?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.118,
            0.203,
            0.775,
            0.238
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "y Prepare a report on IVF, its uses and drawbacks. Discuss it with your class."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.118,
            0.24,
            0.775,
            0.277
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "y Conduct a survey on crop fields. Interact with farmers on the crops grown on their farms and farm animals based on the following points —"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.153,
            0.278,
            0.722,
            0.296
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(i) Which crops do they grow through vegetative propagation?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.148,
            0.295,
            0.543,
            0.312
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(ii) Which crops do they grow using seeds?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.144,
            0.311,
            0.773,
            0.346
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(iii) Which seeds do they use — indigenous varieties or hybrid varieties? Why? How do they develop hybrid varieties in their fields?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.144,
            0.345,
            0.775,
            0.396
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(iv) List the indigenous breeds and hybrid breeds of the farm animals they are using in their farming practices and how are they different from each other?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.148,
            0.396,
            0.773,
            0.431
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(v) Discuss in class, and make a report on how asexual and sexual methods of reproduction are useful in agriculture."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.118,
            0.433,
            0.775,
            0.486
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Explore the crop fields near your school and find out different pollination strategies adopted by different cereal and vegetable crop plants. Talk to farmers on the following points —"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.788,
            0.208,
            0.948,
            0.48
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 12,
              "bbox": [
                0.788,
                0.208,
                0.948,
                0.48
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_19_image_12.jpg",
              "content": ""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.154,
            0.487,
            0.452,
            0.505
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(i) Pollinators of different crops"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.148,
            0.504,
            0.773,
            0.539
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(ii) Reason for the declining population of pollinators and their solutions"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 15,
          "bbox": [
            0.147,
            0.541,
            0.775,
            0.627
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Observe the pollinators visiting your school garden. Notice and record their activity. Let each student take pictures of at least five different types of pollinators and which plants they visit. Compile the data and showcase your work to discuss how pollination occurs in different plants."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 16,
          "bbox": [
            0.118,
            0.629,
            0.775,
            0.698
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "y Assist your elders in cutting fruits in the kitchen. While cutting fruits like lady finger, tomato, brinjal, capsicum, papaya, orange, muskmelon and more, make your observations based on the following and draw diagrams —"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 17,
          "bbox": [
            0.153,
            0.7,
            0.748,
            0.718
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(i) When you cut a fruit longitudinally (Longitudinal Section: L.S.)"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 18,
          "bbox": [
            0.148,
            0.718,
            0.717,
            0.736
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(ii) When you cut a fruit transversely (Transverse Section: T.S.)"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 19,
          "bbox": [
            0.144,
            0.735,
            0.375,
            0.752
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(iii) Attachment of seeds"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 20,
          "bbox": [
            0.797,
            0.489,
            0.94,
            0.58
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
