              "content": ""
            },
            {
              "type": "image_caption",
              "index": 22,
              "bbox": [
                0.792,
                0.588,
                0.958,
                0.604
              ],
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "(a) L.S. of Tomato fruit"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 21,
          "bbox": [
            0.148,
            0.755,
            0.773,
            0.791
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Link your observations of the L.S. and T.S. of the fruit with the internal structure of the ovary of same species."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 23,
          "bbox": [
            0.133,
            0.852,
            0.756,
            0.907
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Does a unicellular organism like amoeba or yeast ever ‘grow old’? When it divides, it produces almost two identical copies. So, does aging happen at all?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
